<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bermudo II of León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 953–999</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bermudo II was King of León from 984 to 999, having first been proclaimed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> in 982 against his cousin Ramiro III. His reign coincided with the height of the power of al-Mansur, the regent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, whose raids sacked León and, in 997, the shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago-de-compostela">Santiago de Compostela</a>, reducing Bermudo to submission and tribute. His son Alfonso V succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bermudo-ii-of-leon.jpg" alt="Bermudo II of León" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bermudo_II_of_Le%C3%B3n.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
